---
import { buildRevision } from "../build";
import trace from "../data/exhibits/decimal-iron-replay.json";

type Props = { id: "three-clocks" | "decimal-iron-replay" | "spa-week" };
const { id } = Astro.props;
const recipes = {
  "three-clocks": {
    note: "three-clocks",
    mutation: "wrong-parser",
    expected:
      "Eleven fixture cases pass. The original calculation is €11,433.07; the corrected parser with the historical reference gives €124.13. Missing historical payloads produce Unavailable.",
    rejection:
      "The mutation uses the original parser for the corrected case. The unchanged expectation requires 12,413 EUR cents; the mutated computation returns 1,143,307. The command must exit 1 at published-corrected-recomputation.",
    browser: "three-clocks",
  },
  "decimal-iron-replay": {
    note: "decimal-iron-replay",
    mutation: "hide-beacon",
    expected:
      "Three recorded scenarios pass their trace checks. The committed payment and its same-identity retry each show one transaction. The EUR discrepancy is 1 cent with the beacon on; fresh reconciliation reduces it to 0 cents with the beacon off.",
    rejection:
      "The mutation switches off the recorded beacon while retaining the assertion that observed it on. The command must exit 1 and identify state.beacon_on. This challenges the trace checker; it does not rerun the payment machine.",
    browser: "decimal-iron-replay",
  },
  "spa-week": {
    note: "size-the-spa-to-the-river",
    mutation: "net-the-week",
    expected:
      "Weekly netting gives 3,640 kWh of imports and no exports. Resolving the same 168 hours gives 6,440 kWh of imports, 2,800 kWh of exports and a 110 kW peak import.",
    rejection:
      "The mutation substitutes weekly netting for the hourly calculation. Its 3,640 kWh import result must fail the unchanged hourly expectation of 6,440 kWh. The command must exit 1 at hourly: energy balance in kWh.",
    browser: "spa-week",
  },
};
const recipe = recipes[id];
const pinned = /^[a-f0-9]{40}$/.test(buildRevision);
const checkout = `git clone --no-checkout https://github.com/bayleafwalker/kotona.app.git kotona-reproduce
cd kotona-reproduce
git checkout --detach ${buildRevision}
node scripts/reproduce-exhibit.mjs ${id}`;
const challenge = `node scripts/reproduce-exhibit.mjs ${id} --mutation ${recipe.mutation}`;
const browser = `npm ci
npx playwright install chromium
npx playwright test tests/browser/${recipe.browser}.spec.mjs`;
const upstream = `git clone --no-checkout https://github.com/bayleafwalker/decimal-iron.git decimal-iron-reproduce
cd decimal-iron-reproduce
git checkout --detach ${trace.implementation.revision}
python3 -m unittest discover -v
python3 -m decimal_iron replay --output artifacts/replay.json
python3 -m decimal_iron replay --check artifacts/replay.json`;
const body = [
  `Note: https://kotona.app/notes/${recipe.note}/`,
  `Site revision: ${buildRevision}`,
  ...(id === "decimal-iron-replay"
    ? [`Python reference revision: ${trace.implementation.revision}`]
    : []),
  "",
  "Case or command:",
  "Expected result:",
  "Observed result:",
  "Runtime and operating system:",
  "Disagreement concerns implementation / claim / applicability:",
  "",
  "Include public or synthetic inputs only; remove credentials and private logs.",
].join("\n");
const reportHref = `mailto:contact@kotona.app?subject=${encodeURIComponent(`Different result: ${id}`)}&body=${encodeURIComponent(body)}`;
---

<section
  class="reproduce-exhibit"
  id="reproduce"
  data-exhibit-reproduction={id}
>
  <p>
    Use Git and Node 24.16 or later within Node 24. The calculation and trace
    checks below use only Node's standard library; no package installation is
    needed. Work in a new directory.
  </p>
  {
    pinned ? (
      <>
        <p>
          This recipe selects the source revision used by this page:{" "}
          <a
            href={`https://github.com/bayleafwalker/kotona.app/commit/${buildRevision}`}
          >
            <code>{buildRevision}</code>
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <pre>
          <code class="language-sh">{checkout}</code>
        </pre>
      </>
    ) : (
      <p>
        This preview has no source revision. Use the published page's pinned
        recipe before treating the result as a reproduction.
      </p>
    )
  }
  <p>
    <strong>Expected result.</strong>
    {recipe.expected} A successful run exits 0.
  </p>
  <h3>Make one wrong change</h3>
  <p>{recipe.rejection}</p>
  <pre><code class="language-sh">{challenge}</code></pre>
  <p>
    The mutation changes a copy in memory and leaves the checked expectations
    untouched. It writes no source or fixture files. Run the first command again
    to return to the unchanged case. Exit 1 must identify the disagreement
    described above. Exit 3 means the mutation escaped its check or execution
    failed elsewhere; it does not establish rejection of the wrong behavior.
  </p>
  {
    id === "decimal-iron-replay" && (
      <details>
        <summary>Rerun the Python payment reference</summary>
        <p>
          Use Python 3.11 or later and Git, in a separate new directory. These
          commands execute the file-backed reference machine, its byte terminal,
          payment adapter, journal replay and three harmful mutations. They need
          no installed packages or running service.
        </p>
        <pre>
          <code class="language-sh">{upstream}</code>
        </pre>
        <p>
          The export must report verification status <code>passed</code>, three
          passed scenarios, and three rejected negative controls. The final
          command executes the cases again and compares the export. Hardware,
          RTL scenario execution and KESKUS remain skipped.
        </p>
        <p>
          To compare the published fixture itself, download its JSON from the
          evidence links below and pass that file to{" "}
          <code>python3 -m decimal_iron replay --check</code>. Object-key order
          and whitespace may differ; the checked values must agree.
        </p>
      </details>
    )
  }
  <details>
    <summary>Check the browser presentation too</summary>
    <p>
      From the same pinned Kotona checkout, install the locked site dependencies
      and Chromium, then run the focused browser checks. These check the
      controls and visible results separately from the calculation or trace
      checks above.
    </p>
    <pre><code class="language-sh">{browser}</code></pre>
  </details>
  <p class="reproduce-report">
    <a href={reportHref}>Report a different result</a>
  </p>
  <p class="reproduce-scope">
    The link opens an email draft with the note and revisions. Add the case,
    expected and observed results, and runtime. A successful reproduction
    establishes these cases under the stated assumptions; the source bindings
    below are not a record of your run.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .reproduce-exhibit {
    margin-block: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .reproduce-exhibit > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .reproduce-exhibit details {
    margin-block: 1.25rem;
  }
  .reproduce-exhibit summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .reproduce-exhibit a code {
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .reproduce-report {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .reproduce-scope {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
